  "title": "Erik the Red's settlement of Greenland",
  "summary": "Outlawed from Iceland for three years, Erik the Red explored Greenland from about 982, then returned to Iceland and led a colonizing fleet in 985. Fourteen of the ships arrived, and the settlers formed an Eastern and a Western Settlement, with Erik's own seat at Brattahlid, now Qassiarsuk.",
