    "uncertainty": {
      "note": "The colonizing voyage is dated summer 985 by the Mariners' Museum and 985 by Visit Greenland, while Encyclopedia.com has Erik back in Iceland in 985 and setting out 'the next year', and also c. 985 in a second entry; it dates the exile to 981 against 982 elsewhere. Ship counts differ: 35 ships (Mariners' Museum) against 25 (Encyclopedia.com, Visit Greenland); all give 14 arriving. The path is left undated because of the conflict."
